4. Enterprise features and activation

"Enterprise Features" means organization and multi-user administration,
enterprise roles and organizational permissions, shared-resource authorization,
SSO, enterprise operation auditing and their associated governance capabilities
identified as Enterprise in the corresponding product release. These obligations
cannot be expanded retroactively for that release. Workspace operation, Agent
execution, files, Git, terminals, personal configuration, templates and internal
hosted conversations are not Enterprise Features merely because EE code is
present. Executing the license verifier in Community state is not Enterprise use.

Except for the isolated activities in Section 3(c) and permitted frozen-state
continuation below, Enterprise Features require a valid Enterprise License
issued by Licensor. "Enterprise License" means the signed activation document
for the authorized enterprise, host, feature scope and validity period. It is the
only enterprise authorization; this license creates no separate commercial,
reseller, hosting, OEM or white-label authorization or additional seat/node limit.

An Enterprise License does not grant redistribution, resale, third-party hosting
or other rights prohibited by Section 5. Public source availability, compiling or
modifying the software, or removing activation checks does not replace the
required Enterprise License. You may not forge or use unauthorized activation
documents, or bypass activation for unlicensed production Enterprise use. Lawful
non-production testing, security research and non-waivable legal rights remain
permitted within Section 3(c).

Expiration does not itself terminate the free Community grant or delete Your
data. For an installation lawfully activated before expiration, continued
internal use of existing configured login, registered Node/Workspace access,
Agent, files, Git, terminals, hosted conversations and audit operation is
permitted in the product's frozen state. Enterprise management writes remain
unlicensed until a valid Enterprise License is obtained. This limited continuation
does not renew the Enterprise License, allow new management permissions or permit
circumventing the management freeze. No new remote shutdown obligation is created.

