9. Breach and termination

If You violate this license, Your rights under it terminate and You must stop the
violating activity immediately. If a non-deliberate, remediable breach is Your
first breach, rights are reinstated when You fully remedy it within 30 days after
receiving notice from Licensor. This cure period permits no continued unlicensed
Enterprise use, distribution or third-party operation. Deliberate activation
forgery or circumvention and repeated breaches have no automatic reinstatement.
Reinstatement does not grant any rights prohibited by Section 5.

After termination, cease uses no longer permitted by this license. You may retain
copies strictly required by applicable law and make copies necessary to export
Your own data, but may not use them for further operation or distribution.
Independent component licenses are not terminated by this provision. License
expiration alone is governed by Section 4, not this breach provision.

